Drop setup_requires=['pytest-runner'].

setuptools treats setup_requires as an implicit dependency to be fetched before
the build starts. Inside the Nix sandbox there is no network access, so the
build fails while trying to download pytest-runner. The requirement only drives
`python setup.py test`, which this package never runs: the wheel is built with
bdist_wheel and installed with `installer`, neither of which touches it.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -305,7 +305,6 @@ def get_version():
     url='https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmcv',
     author='MMCV Authors',
     author_email='openmmlab@gmail.com',
-    setup_requires=['pytest-runner'],
     tests_require=['pytest'],
     install_requires=install_requires,
     ext_modules=get_extensions(),
